    {
      question: "We have never looked at security formally. Where do we start?",
      answer: "Start with a Discovery Audit. It costs $750 plus GST and is credited in full against the build. It sets out the risks we find across your product, including security, and assesses it against recognised standards, so you know where the highest risk gaps are before anything is built or changed. If you also want an independent penetration test of an existing system, we can help you find a specialist firm.",
    },
    {
      question: "What happens if there is a security incident?",
      answer: "If a system we built or support has a security problem, contact us and we will work with you to contain it and fix the cause in the software. We do not run an incident response team or forensic investigations; for a serious breach, engage a specialist incident response firm. Whether you must notify anyone under the Notifiable Data Breaches scheme in the Privacy Act 1988 is a question for your lawyer, and the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner publishes guidance on it.",
    },
    {
      question: "What is secure software development?",
      answer: "Secure software development means building security into every stage of the software lifecycle, from design and threat modelling through code review, dependency scanning and security testing to deployment and monitoring, instead of testing for problems only at the end. Frameworks such as the NIST Secure Software Development Framework and the OWASP guidance describe the practices; we apply them in our own delivery and can help your team adopt them.",
    },
